Fault injection and old-client result
  The old-primary statement executed the real hybrid_search_v2 and then
  pg_sleep(30) before emitting its first result row. pg_stat_activity proved
  P36_FAILOVER_INFLIGHT count=1 and state=active.
  The isolated old primary was stopped with:
    gs_ctl stop -w -t 30 -m immediate
  stop exit: 0
  old client exit: 2
  old client terminal output after the three SET acknowledgements:
    connection to server was lost
  result_record/id rows observed by old client: 0

  P3-5 separately proves cancellation while both producer workers themselves
  are delayed. P3-6 deliberately tests the HA/client boundary after a real
  HybridRecall statement and before first-row delivery; it does not claim that
  SQL pg_sleep is a worker-overlap hook.

