Semantic conclusion
  1. A hot standby can execute the read-only HybridRecall path in this build,
     but the V1 support contract remains centered on the primary.
  2. There is no transparent session/statement migration. Connection loss is
     an error; clients must discard every row from that attempt and retry the
     complete idempotent SELECT on a confirmed read-write primary.
  3. A retry opens a new statement snapshot. Results may legitimately differ
     if WAL/data/index visibility changed across failover; the frozen fixture
     returned byte-for-byte identical IDs.
  4. Session GUCs and prepared plans do not migrate. Reconnect logic must
     reapply HybridRecall GUCs and prepare again. Supplying query_vector avoids
     invoking an external embedding service twice during retry.
